@inject NavigationManager Navigation

@*
    Sends an unauthenticated visitor to sign in.

    This used to append a returnUrl of its own, and nothing has ever read one: signing in always
    lands on the dashboard. A parameter that is written, echoed in the address bar and never
    acted on is worse than none - it reads like a working feature, and the next person to make
    it work would be building an open redirect into a sign-in page without noticing that is what
    they were doing.

    The cookie handler still appends its own ReturnUrl when it redirects, and that one is always
    a local path the framework produced rather than anything a request supplied. It is also
    still not read. If the office wants to be returned to the page they asked for, it needs
    adding deliberately, with the destination checked against Akiba's own base path.
*@

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized() =>
        Navigation.NavigateTo("/sign-in", forceLoad: true);
}
